WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.401
New tonight, the U.S.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:04.804
military failed to flag an early
warning about the Chinese spy balloon

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.640
as an urgent matter as it headed towards
the United States.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.711
Sources say top defense and intelligence
officials who saw the internal alert

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.581
on January 27th weren't immediately
alarmed by it.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:17.317
It was the day
before the balloon crossed into Alaska.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.653
The urgency inside the military
did not change until the spy balloon

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.990
moved over Alaska and headed on a path
clearly towards the continental U.S..

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.992
That is when fighter jets were scrambled.

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:30.196
Now, all of this news coming a day after
President Biden called out the Chinese

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.299
President, Xi Jinping
during the State of the Union address.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.470
Let's be clear.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.739
Winning
the competition should unite all of us.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.675
We face serious
challenges across the world.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:46.846
But in the past two years, democracies
have become stronger, not weaker.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.249
Autocracies grown weaker, not stronger.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:53.887
Name me a world leader
who changed places with Xi Jinping.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.623
Name me one name me one

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.760
Selina Wang is OUTFRONT in Beijing.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.063
Selina, pretty incredible, right, Naomi?

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:06.232
What did the passion,
the force behind that pointing?

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:11.271
And how was that seen by Xi Jinping
and the Chinese government?

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.106
What's the response

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.311
Yeah, Erin, I mean, that was probably
one of the most fiery parts of the speech.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.313
He was practically shouting
by the end of it.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:24.317
And Beijing's response to the speech
has been that the US is smearing

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.720
China under the, quote,
pretext of competition.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.891
And so really, in addition
to directly calling out Xi Jinping,

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:35.261
Biden had also really underscored
for this rhetoric

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.464
that autocracies have grown weaker
around the world.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:38.731
And we've seen his administration

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:42.268
really pose this challenge
as autocracies versus democracies.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.070
Now, China's Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.907
in response to the speech, also said
that they don't want the entire US-China

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.878
relationship defined by competition
from Beijing's perspective.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.546
That speech underscores our view.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.716
America is trying to keep China down
and contain its rise.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.151
They really see Biden

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:02.388
as building on top of former President
Donald Trump's harsher stance on China.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:06.392
They've seen the Biden administration
drop these broad new laws and policies

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:10.196
that challenge China's influence,
for instance, those sweeping restrictions

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:13.666
from the Biden administration
that chokes off China's access to advanced

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:17.437
computer chips and stronger alliances
between the US and other countries

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.272
that they see as anti-China.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:22.041
Interestingly, also during a speech,
Biden talked about investing

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.245
in semiconductor production
at home, bringing back supply chains.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:29.249
Beijing accused the US of undermining
global supply chains Erin.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:29.949
All right.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.919
So anyway,
thank you very much. Live from Beijing.

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:35.822
And I want to go now to the retired Army
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.225
And General Hertling, you know,
the context around this is all this

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.995
new reporting
we're getting on these five balloon

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.864
I guess, for lack of a better word
program of China.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.366
The State Department confirming today

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:50.303
that this Chinese surveillance program
extends far beyond the United States.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.272
What more can you tell us about it?

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.674
Well, you know, first,

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.644
Erin, I go back to what you said
at the very beginning about the military

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:01.614
failing to flag the balloon
going over Alaska as an urgent matter

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.082
I'm not sure I agree with that.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:08.221
You know, the temper that some of our
reporters talked about in a recent article

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:13.293
in dot com talked about information
that was provided to the command

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.031
about this balloon coming across
the Aleutians and going into Africa.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.900
Now, I hate to do this to you, Erin,
but I'll give you a little

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.704
hierarchy of military information
and organizations.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:30.343
There is an organization called Alaska
Command in it's near Anchorage, actually,

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.814
and they have a responsibility as part of
Northern Command, the command that

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:40.320
eventually shot down this balloon
of kind of guarding the coastline.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.690
They have an Air Force base
with the 11th Air Force there.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.758
They have 18 different radar stations.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.895
So when a balloon like that comes over,
they're going to tip on it

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.898
and send that
into the Defense Intelligence Agency.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:55.201
So it goes out in something
that I, as a commander and all other

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.104
commanders get on a daily basis,
call a black book.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:01.941
And until something becomes important,
you don't do anything about it.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.778
The military has a phrase
called owner observe and report.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:10.049
If there's a danger associated with
something, then you do something about it.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:14.020
But when you're just observing it
and tracking it and they had fine

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.091
control of this as it moved,
it crossed Alaska, then into Canada,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:21.894
a different nation and coordination
with Canada then into the United States.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:25.598
I think that's when it started to rise
to the level that

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.234
the Joint Chiefs of Staff
heard about the intelligence.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.036
And then the president eventually did

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.672
right and of course,
now they know the signature of it.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.975
It appears that this had happened
multiple times before.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.945
I'm sure there's a lot of questions
being asked right now.

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.713
And one of the ways

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.982
that they're going to get some answers,
perhaps, is by seeing the payload,

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.718
which, of course, landed off the South
Carolina coast when they took it down.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.854
Now, we understand, General, that the U.S.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.556
military has recovered
most of the debris now from the surface.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.492
They're now going to the underwater
wreckage

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.294
to try to get everything they can.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.962
Right, because that's the whole point.
You're going to take it down.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.164
You want any information
you're able to get.

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:01.868
What are you hearing about
what we might learn about

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:05.271
the balloons capability from what's now
sitting at the bottom of the ocean?

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.041
Yeah, I'm hearing we're learning a lot.

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:08.808
Now, of course, Erin,

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:12.011
I have to comment that
I don't have classified clearance anymore,

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.881
but I am hearing from some of my friends
in the Navy, in the Air Force,

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.884
and they're talking
about the kinds of things they're finding.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:22.021
So not only was this this balloon jammed

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.858
and tracked across the United States to
it could not collect data,

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:29.629
but the data collectors that did have on
board, we're really looking

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:33.633
at electronic surveillance
and signal server surveillance.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.535
And it was a big platform,

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.705
but it was jammed the entire time
it was going across the United States.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:43.076
So we learned a lot about what
it was trying to report back to China.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.179
Also the fact that it certainly
was not a weather balloon.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.115
But as we collect the data
from the ocean floor,

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.217
off the coast of Carolina
and the Carolinas,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.719
I think we're going to learn a whole lot

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:54.754
more about the equipment
that the Chinese used.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:58.558
And by the way, this
this gave us a whole lot of information

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:01.260
on a lot of the other balloons
that they're using

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:05.598
in other areas of the world
to include and most importantly, Taiwan.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.166
Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:07.967
All right, General Hertling,

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:10.670
thank you so much
and for sharing all that new information.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.038
Much appreciated.

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:13.439
Pleasure.

